; TS2Python.def — force undecorated export names for EL's DefineDLLFunc.
;
; Why: on x86 with __stdcall + __declspec(dllexport), MSVC decorates exports
; as _Name@N (e.g. _EL_Init@4). EasyLanguage's DefineDLLFunc / GetProcAddress
; looks up the raw "EL_Init" name and fails. Listing exports here makes the
; linker emit them under the plain symbol name while keeping the __stdcall
; call convention intact.
;
; Keep this in sync with include/ts2python.h.
;
; EL_Init, EL_Init2, EL_PublishTick and EL_PublishBar are TOMBSTONES — they return -6 and initialise
; nothing. They must stay listed here. Dropping them would make an .ELD
; built against the superseded protocol fail at DefineDLLFunc resolution
; with no explanation, whereas returning -6 puts a readable line in
; TradeStation's Print Log. See ../contract/error_codes.md.

LIBRARY TS2Python
EXPORTS
    EL_Init3
    EL_Init
    EL_Init2
    EL_Publish
    EL_PublishTick
    EL_PublishBar
    EL_Shutdown
    EL_DllVersion
